==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Etymology===
From {{inh|en|enm|tankard|tan(c)kard(e)}}, denoting 'a large tub for carrying liquid', perhaps related to {{der|en|nl|tanckaert}}, from {{der|en|dum|tanckaert}},  meaning the same thing, but of uncertain ultimate origin. The OED suggests an alteration of {{der|en|ML.|*kantard}}, from {{der|en|la|cantharus|t=tankard}}.<ref>{{R:OED}}</ref> Klein suggests {{der|en|fr|tant}} {{m|fr|quart|t=as much of a quarter}}.<ref>Klein, Dr. Ernest, A Comprehensive Etymological Dictionary of the English Language, Amsterdam: Elsevier Scientific Publishing Co., 1971</ref>

Meaning "drinking vessel" is first recorded late 15th century.

